# Apache rules for the Django side on shared hosting. Two blocks, two different places.
# Upload as a file literally named .htaccess. Whether a Passenger-routed domain honours
# these at all is host-dependent, so after installing each one, prove it with an anonymous
# request (curl -I https://api.mantbridges.com/<path>) and confirm you get 403 or 404.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Put this in the Application root (the directory holding manage.py) if that
#    directory is reachable over the web at all. The database, the secrets file and
#    the source must never be downloadable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<FilesMatch "\.(sqlite3|sqlite3-journal|env|key|pem|py|pyc|log)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

<Files ".htaccess">
  Require all denied
</Files>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Put this in the MEDIA directory (backend/media/.htaccess).
#
#    Receipt PDFs and chat attachments are saved inside MEDIA_ROOT next to the
#    property photographs, which are meant to be public. The API gates them properly
#    (/api/receipts/{id}/download/ checks the role) but a direct file URL does not go
#    through the API, and the filenames are sequential receipt numbers, so they are
#    guessable: /media/receipts/.../MB-RCP-2026-00017.pdf.
#
#    This blocks those two subtrees and leaves the photographs alone. It is a stopgap;
#    BACKEND_FOLLOWUPS.md 19 is the permanent fix (documents out of the media tree).
#    If the photographs and documents must stay on one host, this rule is what keeps the
#    money documents private.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

RewriteEngine On
RewriteRule ^(receipts|messages|avatars)(/|$) - [F,L]
